---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe30.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope – the Complete Set of Financial Statements" },
        { id: "s3", label: "General Principles" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Balance Sheet – Classified Presentation" },
        { id: "s5", label: "THE PRESENTATION DIFFERENCE – a Mandatory Single Income Statement" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Going Concern and Accrual Basis" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Offsetting Restrictions" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example – the Single-Statement Income Statement Structure" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example – Current vs Non-Current Classification" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS 1" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The general framework governing the primary statements</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 30 establishes the GENERAL requirements for the PRESENTATION of FINANCIAL statements – GOVERNING structure, CONTENT, and MINIMUM line ITEMS across the FOUR primary STATEMENTS plus NOTES, BROADLY converged with IAS 1 internationally, WITH one NOTABLE presentation-STRUCTURE difference (Section 5).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – the Complete Set of Financial Statements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Balance Sheet, Income Statement, Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity, Cash Flow Statement, and Notes</div><div class="principle">A COMPLETE set of FINANCIAL statements COMPRISES a BALANCE Sheet, an INCOME Statement, a STATEMENT of CHANGES in Owners' EQUITY, a CASH Flow STATEMENT, and ACCOMPANYING notes – CONSISTENT with IAS 1'S own REQUIRED set of PRIMARY statements internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>General Principles</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair presentation, consistency, materiality, comparability</div><div class="text-supporting">FINANCIAL statements must FAIRLY present the ENTERPRISE'S financial POSITION, performance, and CASH flows, APPLYING accounting POLICIES CONSISTENTLY, WITH materiality GUIDING the LEVEL of AGGREGATION and DISCLOSURE, and COMPARATIVE information PRESENTED for the PRIOR period, CONSISTENT with IAS 1'S own GENERAL principles internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Balance Sheet – Classified Presentation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Current/non-current distinction</div><div class="text-supporting">The BALANCE Sheet is PRESENTED using a CLASSIFIED structure, DISTINGUISHING CURRENT from NON-CURRENT assets and LIABILITIES – CONSISTENT with IAS 1'S own CLASSIFIED presentation APPROACH internationally (WITH an UNCLASSIFIED, liquidity-ORDERED presentation ALSO permitted WHERE it PROVIDES more RELIABLE and RELEVANT information, AS under IAS 1).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE PRESENTATION DIFFERENCE – a Mandatory Single Income Statement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">One combined statement, not a choice between one or two</div><div class="text-supporting">ASBE No. 30 REQUIRES a SINGLE, combined INCOME Statement PRESENTING BOTH net PROFIT and OTHER comprehensive INCOME TOGETHER, ENDING in a "TOTAL comprehensive INCOME" figure – WHEREAS IAS 1 PERMITS a CHOICE BETWEEN this SAME single-STATEMENT approach OR presenting NET profit and OTHER comprehensive INCOME as TWO separate STATEMENTS. This is a NARROW, but GENUINE, presentation-level DIVERGENCE – ASBE MANDATES the single-STATEMENT format, RATHER than LEAVING it as an ELECTIVE choice.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Going Concern and Accrual Basis</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The two foundational assumptions</div><div class="text-supporting">FINANCIAL statements are PREPARED on the ASSUMPTION the ENTERPRISE is a GOING concern (UNLESS management INTENDS or is FORCED to LIQUIDATE or CEASE trading), and on the ACCRUAL basis of ACCOUNTING (RECOGNISING transactions WHEN they OCCUR, RATHER than WHEN cash is RECEIVED or PAID) – CONSISTENT with IAS 1'S own FOUNDATIONAL assumptions.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Offsetting Restrictions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Assets and liabilities, income and expenses, presented separately</div><div class="text-supporting">ASSETS and LIABILITIES, and INCOME and EXPENSES, are NOT offset AGAINST each OTHER UNLESS SPECIFICALLY required or PERMITTED by another ASBE standard – CONSISTENT with IAS 1'S own OFFSETTING restriction internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example – the Single-Statement Income Statement Structure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">One combined statement ending in total comprehensive income</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Combining net profit and OCI in one statement</div><div class="wk-body">A company reports net profit of RMB 40,000,000 for the year, plus RMB 5,000,000 of foreign currency translation gains recognised within other comprehensive income.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company presents BOTH figures WITHIN a SINGLE Income STATEMENT, ENDING in TOTAL comprehensive INCOME of RMB 40,000,000 + RMB 5,000,000 = <strong>RMB 45,000,000</strong> – RATHER than PRESENTING net PROFIT and OCI as TWO separate statements (an OPTION IAS 1 would PERMIT, but ASBE does NOT).</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example – Current vs Non-Current Classification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Splitting the Balance Sheet by expected settlement timing</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Classifying a long-term loan's current portion</div><div class="wk-body">A company has a 5-year bank loan, with RMB 8,000,000 due for repayment within the next 12 months and the remaining RMB 32,000,000 due thereafter.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company CLASSIFIES RMB 8,000,000 as a CURRENT liability and RMB 32,000,000 as a NON-CURRENT liability, REFLECTING the CLASSIFIED Balance Sheet PRESENTATION this Standard REQUIRES.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 30 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>A complete set of financial statements, with comparative prior period information</span><span>Significant accounting policies and judgements applied</span><span>Basis of preparation, including confirmation of the going concern assumption</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Assessing whether the going concern assumption remains appropriate</span><span>Determining materiality for presentation and disclosure purposes</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classification of assets and liabilities as current or non-current where settlement timing is uncertain</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 1</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison – ASBE 30 vs IAS 1</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 30</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 1</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Net profit/OCI presentation</span><span>MANDATORY single combined statement</span><span>CHOICE – single statement OR two separate statements</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Classified Balance Sheet</span><span>Standard approach, with an unclassified alternative</span><span>Standard approach, with an unclassified alternative – converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, WITH the SINGLE-statement MANDATE being the ONLY notable, NARROW point of PRESENTATION-level divergence.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where this Standard's own requirements apply</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Overall presentation structure</span><span>ALL primary statements</span><span>Governs the complete set of financial statements</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 31</span><span>Cash Flow Statements – supplies the detailed requirements for the fourth primary statement this Standard requires</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 29</span><span>Events after the Balance Sheet Date – relevant for the going concern assessment this Standard requires</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Total comprehensive income</div><div class="glossary-def">The combined total of net profit and other comprehensive income, presented within a single mandatory Income Statement under ASBE.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Classified Balance Sheet</div><div class="glossary-def">A Balance Sheet presentation distinguishing current from non-current assets and liabilities.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe30 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
